<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as SBY</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono is a retired Indonesian general and politician who served as president from 2004 to 2014. A former security minister, he founded the Democratic Party and won the country's first direct presidential election in 2004. His two terms brought steady growth, the 2005 peace agreement that ended the conflict in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> and an anti-corruption drive, and he was the first Indonesian president to hand over power at the end of his constitutional term.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/susilo-bambang-yudhoyono.jpg" alt="Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Indonesia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Susilo_Bambang_Yudhoyono,_official_presidential_portrait_(2009).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
